@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Brwsl tab lifecycle (lazy WebView realization)

[*] --> Start : application activate
Start --> Restoring : restore_session and stored rows exist
Start --> Placeholder : start URL or first tab
Restoring --> Placeholder : create_page(url) per row

state Placeholder {
  [*] --> PageArea
  PageArea : page area and status line\nno WebKit view yet
}

Placeholder --> Realizing : tab selected
Realizing --> Loading : WebView::load_uri(url)
Loading --> Ready : LoadEvent::Finished
Loading --> Failed : page load error
Ready --> Failed : address rejected by policy
Failed --> Loading : corrected address
Ready --> Ready : tab reselected, WebView kept alive
Ready --> Loading : the window's address field or a button
Ready --> Closing : close requested
Loading --> Closing : close requested
Closing --> Empty : it was the last remaining tab
Empty --> Placeholder : reset to about:blank, keep the window
Closing --> [*] : window closed, session saved

note bottom of Placeholder
  A WebView is created only when a tab is
  first selected. Private tabs share one
  ephemeral NetworkSession and are never
  written to the session database.
end note
@enduml
